  "title": "Generalized holographic principle",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "9a3de36f-24b9-4d5b-b79a-d6156a23ed6e",
      "text": "If a finite closed system is split into two separable parts, the classical information they exchange is limited to N bits, where N is the dimension of their interaction Hamiltonian. Informally, classical information exchanged between finite systems is encoded on the boundary between them.",
